cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this note or its computations, please cite it as below.
  Please also cite the OpenAI preprint listed in UPSTREAM.md.
type: software
title: 'An explicit prime range for the height-two counterexamples to the Hahn-Wilson conjecture'
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-09'
authors:
  - name: '[AUTHOR NAME]'
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  OpenAI's preprint constructs counterexamples to the Hahn-Wilson conjecture at
  height two for every sufficiently large prime p. Its parameter conditions
  first hold at p = 17,073,437. Choosing one parameter differently, with the
  argument otherwise unchanged, makes the construction work for every prime
  p >= 293, and 293 is the least prime this argument can reach (199 and 211
  are added by a sharper reading of one step). This is a re-tuning of constants
  with no new idea; it is conditional on the correctness of the upstream
  preprint. Found and checked by Claude (Anthropic) agents under the
  repository owner's direction. No human peer review has taken place and
  nothing is formalized in Lean; no historical-priority claim is made.
keywords:
  - Hahn-Wilson conjecture
  - chromatic homotopy theory
  - truncated Brown-Peterson spectra
  - explicit bounds
references:
